Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:42:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: vxd: Add the H.264 CAVLC table from the
 Imagination VXD source
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The MSVDX entropy decoder reads a packed CAVLC table that the host
uploads with every slice. Take it from the GPL-2.0 Imagination/Texas
Instruments VXD decoder (img-vxe-vxd decoder/h264_vlc.h, by Angela
Stegmaier, commit 9453ad8ebdd4), which TI also carries in its kernel as
drivers/media/platform/vxe-vxd/decoder/h264_vlc.h.

Keep the upstream file verbatim with its notices in upstream/h264_vlc.h,
and the offline generator h264-tables.py that packs its 544 triples as
opcode << 12 | width << 9 | symbol into apple-vxd-h264-tables.h. The
generated table reproduces all 544 entries and has CRC-32 0xa0d60f2e,
which the driver checks when it uploads the table. No Apple binary is an
input.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
